// Drive force on an axle. Open: both sides always get the same torque, so the wheel with less grip limits both.
// Limited-slip (bias > 1): friction plates between a side gear and the carrier resist the two sides turning apart, so
// while one wheel slips the other can take up to `bias` times its torque (the torque bias ratio). Locked: the axle turns
// as one shaft and each wheel can push up to its own grip.
